{
  "id": "reverse_vowels_of_a_string",
  "title": "Reverse Vowels of a String",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Algorithms",
  "tags": [
    "Two Pointers",
    "String"
  ],
  "description": "<p>Given a string <code>s</code>, reverse only all the vowels in the string and return it.</p> <p>The vowels are <code>'a'</code>, <code>'e'</code>, <code>'i'</code>, <code>'o'</code>, and <code>'u'</code>, and they can appear in both lower and upper cases, more than once.</p> <p> </p> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p> <div class=\"example-block\"> <p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">s = \"IceCreAm\"</span></p> <p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">\"AceCreIm\"</span></p> <p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p> <p>The vowels in <code>s</code> are <code>['I', 'e', 'e', 'A']</code>. On reversing the vowels, s becomes <code>\"AceCreIm\"</code>.</p> </div> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p> <div class=\"example-block\"> <p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">s = \"leetcode\"</span></p> <p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">\"leotcede\"</span></p> </div> <p> </p> <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>1 &lt;= s.length &lt;= 3 * 10<sup>5</sup></code></li> <li><code>s</code> consist of <strong>printable ASCII</strong> characters.</li> </ul>",
  "hints": [],
  "method": {
    "name": "reverseVowels",
    "returnType": "auto",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "s",
        "type": "string"
